  "problem_statement": "Bag distance algorithm returns incorrect values for identical and similar strings\n\n#### Description\n\nThe Bag distance algorithm is returning unexpected values when comparing strings. For identical strings like 'qwe' and 'qwe', it returns 3 instead of the expected 0. Similarly, for anagrams like 'qwe' and 'ewq', it also returns 3 instead of 0.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport textdistance\n\n# Test with identical strings\nresult1 = textdistance.bag('qwe', 'qwe')\nprint(f\"bag('qwe', 'qwe') = {result1}\")  # Expected: 0, Actual: 3\n\n# Test with anagrams (same characters, different order)\nresult2 = textdistance.bag('qwe', 'ewq') \nprint(f\"bag('qwe', 'ewq') = {result2}\")  # Expected: 0, Actual: 3\n\n# Test with completely different strings\nresult3 = textdistance.bag('qwe', 'rtys')\nprint(f\"bag('qwe', 'rtys') = {result3}\")  # Expected: 4, Actual: 3\n```\n\nThe bag distance should return 0 for identical strings and anagrams since they contain the same character frequencies, but it's currently returning incorrect values.",
